        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Red House Painters, Daughtry\n- People: Gorden Mack, Phil Carney, Chris Daughtry, Billy Anderson\n- Places: San Francisco, California\n- Events: Break the Spell Tour\n- Topics: American rock bands, music production, touring\n\nFacts:\n- Red House Painters were an American rock band formed in San Francisco, California, in 1988.\n- Gorden Mack performed with Red House Painters during a six-year tenure.\n- Phil Carney performed with Red House Painters during a separate six-year tenure.\n- Chris Daughtry was a finalist on the fifth season of American Idol.\n- Daughtry is an American rock band formed and fronted by Chris Daughtry.\n- Billy Anderson worked with hundreds of bands over 29 years, including Red House Painters, Neurosis, Swans, Melvins, Jawbreaker, Sleep, Brutal Truth, Buzzoven, Fantômas, Agalloch, Cattle Decapitation, Mr. Bungle, and Asunder.\n- Break the Spell Tour was the second headlining tour by Daughtry.",
